  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/channa_stewartii_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>This snakehead, often traded under the name Channa cf. barca, originates from the Indian province of Assam. Channa stewartii can reach a length of 30 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/channa_stewartii_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>India, Assam.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/channa_stewartii_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>For a pair, a well-planted 200 l aquarium with slow-moving water and some hiding places would be ideal.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/channa_stewartii_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>Since their habitat does not lie in the tropical range, they can be kept well in an unheated aquarium. They tolerate temperatures between 20–30°C and have low requirements concerning other water parameters. They can tolerate low-oxygen conditions in water because they are air breathers from an early age.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/channa_stewartii_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>Besides live and dead fish, they accept food such as insects, worms and, after habituation, possibly also sticks.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/channa_stewartii_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>As predators they should be kept together only with fishes whose length is at least 2/3 of their own body length.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25a-perchlike-fishes-1-labyrinth-fishes/channa_stewartii_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>Channa stewartii is probably a nest builder providing eggs and young with parental care. Other reports mention them as mouthbrooders.</p>"
    }
  ],
